//! Charter `H-REGISTRY` models, generated by
//! `proptest_scheduler_region_split_registry`.
//!
//! The property drives the real declaration-only aggregation seam:
//! `slicer_scheduler::region_split::aggregate_region_splits` and its separate
//! `slicer_scheduler::region_split::canonical_variant_chain_order` helper, plus
//! the real plan-assembly caller
//! (`slicer_scheduler::execution_plan::build_execution_plan`, which stores the
//! aggregate in `ExecutionPlan.aggregated_region_split`).
//!
//! The independent model is relational, not a copy of the aggregator:
//!
//! * a repeated semantic is compatible exactly when every declaration agrees on
//!   `(priority, value_type)`; one entry is derived per semantic as
//!   `(priority, value_type, sorted distinct declaring_modules)`;
//! * the expected aggregate contains precisely the generated declarations — no
//!   `material`/`fuzzy_skin` seed exists unless a module declares it;
//! * the expected raw-key order is semantic-name order, while the expected
//!   helper sequence is the separate `(priority, name)` sort;
//! * deliberately incompatible repeats are explicitly order-sensitive: a linear
//!   positional scan keeps the first-seen contract and emits one warning for
//!   every later incompatible declaration;
//! * one nonfatal tied-priority warning is derived per priority shared by two
//!   or more distinct semantics, using the spec's exact payload wording.
//!
//! `tests/property_scheduler_contracts.rs` mounts this module for the
//! deterministic controls, so every helper here is a plain target-private test
//! module, not a new SDK API. The direct helper assertion is **not** evidence
//! that `RegionMapping` uses the helper: `canonical_variant_chain_order` has no
//! production caller in this tree (see ADR-0018's amendment).

#![allow(dead_code)]

